window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-6f03fc40590b30ca"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"plan-a-budget-and-schedule\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">规划预算与日程</h1> <p>把时间冲突、工作量集中、账单与预算放在一起看。</p> <p>结合课程日历、工作班次、固定安排、收入、支出和账单，生成每周规划仪表板、冲突视图、预算跟踪器和可调整的行动计划。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要平衡课程、工作班次、固定安排和账单的学生。</li> <li>既要考虑时间限制，也要考虑资金限制的每周计划。</li> <li>希望仪表板提出可选方案，但不直接修改日程或发起交易的规划任务。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>构建可编辑的预算、日程和待付款项仪表板。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>google-calendar</code></td> <td>读取经批准的课程、工作和固定日历安排。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>创建我的预算与日程仪表板</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">根据我的课程日历、工作班次、固定安排、收入、支出类别和账单，构建个人规划仪表板。\n\n请展示：\n- 每周时间冲突\n- 工作量集中时段\n- 即将到期的付款\n- 可调整的预算视图\n- 下一周切实可行的选项\n\n不要修改日历事件、发送消息、进行金融交易，也不要猜测缺失的收入或支出。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"combine-only-the-planning-data-you-need\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">只整合规划所需的数据</h2> <p>请提供规划时间范围内需要考虑的课程日历、工作班次、固定安排、账单、收入和支出类别。移除账号号码等敏感财务细节。</p> <p>确认日期范围、货币、发薪频率，以及哪些安排是固定的、哪些可以调整。</p> <p><a id=\"build-an-adjustable-dashboard\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">创建可调整的仪表板</h2> <p>使用起始提示词创建：</p> <ol> <li>标出重叠安排的每周日程。</li> <li>显示截止日期和工作班次聚集的时段。</li> <li>制作简明的收入与支出计划。</li> <li>列出已核实日期的近期账单。</li> <li>比较调整可自由支配时间或支出的情景。</li> </ol> <p>清楚区分来源数据、假设和建议。</p> <p><a id=\"review-before-acting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">行动前先核对</h2> <p>对照原始来源检查每一笔账单和每条日历事项。不要把估算费用或未经确认的班次当成确定信息。</p> <p>用计划来比较选项，而不是自动替你作决定。ChatGPT 不应修改日历事项、联系任何人、转移资金或进行购买。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"plan-a-budget-and-schedule\">Plan a budget and schedule</h1> <p>See time conflicts, workload clusters, bills, and budget together.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with course calendars, work shifts, recurring commitments, income, expenses, and bills to create a weekly planning dashboard, conflict view, budget tracker, and adjustable action plan.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Students balancing classes, work shifts, commitments, and bills.</li> <li>Weekly plans that need both time and money constraints.</li> <li>Dashboards that suggest options without changing events or making transactions.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Build an editable budget, schedule, and upcoming-payments dashboard.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>google-calendar</code></td> <td>Read approved course, work, and recurring calendar commitments.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build My Budget and Schedule Dashboard</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Build a personal planning dashboard from my course calendar, work shifts, recurring commitments, income, expense categories, and bills.\n\nShow:\n- weekly time conflicts\n- major workload clusters\n- upcoming payments\n- an adjustable budget view\n- practical options for the next week\n\nDo not change calendar events, send messages, make financial transactions, or assume missing income or expenses.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"combine-only-the-planning-data-you-need\">Combine only the planning data you need</h2> <p>Provide the course calendar, work shifts, recurring commitments, bills, income, and expense categories that belong in the planning window. Remove account numbers and other sensitive financial details.</p> <p>Confirm the date range, currency, pay schedule, and which commitments are fixed or flexible.</p> <h2 id=\"build-an-adjustable-dashboard\">Build an adjustable dashboard</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt to create:</p> <ol> <li>A weekly schedule with overlapping commitments highlighted.</li> <li>A workload view for clustered deadlines and shifts.</li> <li>A simple income and expense plan.</li> <li>An upcoming-bills list with verified dates.</li> <li>Scenarios for changing discretionary time or spending.</li> </ol> <p>Keep source values, assumptions, and suggestions visibly separate.</p> <h2 id=\"review-before-acting\">Review before acting</h2> <p>Check every bill and calendar entry against its original source. Make sure the dashboard does not treat estimated costs or unconfirmed shifts as fixed.</p> <p>Use the plan to compare options, not to automate decisions. ChatGPT should not change events, contact anyone, move money, or make purchases.</p>"};
